# 312 — The Mind's memory: a journal, assertions and derived indexes — done

**Type:** main task · **Owner:** `STO` track · **Priority:** P2 · **Status:** done (2026-11-13) · **Blocked by:** — ([308](308-encryption-at-rest.done), sealing before personal data, is done); for its QEMU criterion, a program started in a memory domain ([312-APP-0134](312-APP-0134-a-program-started-in-a-memory-domain.done)) · **Roadmap:** track B "assertions and derived indexes" · **Constitution:** MC-4.5, MC-4.7, MC-4.8, MC-4.11, MC-4.12, MC-10.3, MC-11.5, Appendix B.3

From the kernel session's draft (`STO/2026-10-25T1557Z-KRN-draft-plan-the-store-as-a-minds-memory.md` on `internal-dev-messages`), taken by the storage session at the maintainer's word (2026-10-27). Everything here is plan, not a guarantee (MC-12.3).

## Problem

A Mind needs memory with an explicit history, deliberate and accounted forgetting, and indexes that never become authority. The store keeps objects and names, but no journal, no assertions about objects and no indexes over them.

## Plan

- **The journal**, append-only per memory domain: each entry is an object (a monotonic time and the calendar time with its source; the source program and its identity from the badge; a kind; the content's CID; a link to the entry before). The head is published by compare-and-swap, so a reader checks order and completeness from it.
- **Assertions**, apart from content (MC-4.12): a claim about an object, its subject's CID, its author and its origin; signed where it crosses a trust zone (B.3); each kind of metadata names its source of truth.
- **Derived indexes:** full text; and vectors.
  - **Who does what** (the storage session's choice, 2026-10-27): `NRL`'s runtime computes the embeddings; this track keeps the index. Its manifest names the model's CID and the index's parameters, so it can be rebuilt and a stale one detected.
  - **The structure:** an exact scan first; an approximate index such as HNSW when the sizes ask for it, with recall measured against the exact scan.
  - An index is never authority or proof that a version is current, and may be dropped and rebuilt (MC-4.12).
- **Retention and forgetting:** each domain has an owner, a term and a quota (MC-4.11); "forget" removes the names and collects; "forget for sure" destroys the domain's key ([308](308-encryption-at-rest.done)); copies already handed over are outside both, and that is said (MC-4.8).
- **Rights and data:** a memory domain is a capability, and an agent (260) holds its own only; text read from memory is data, never an instruction (MC-11.5).

## Tasks

- [312-STO-0034](312-STO-0034-a-journal-checked-from-its-head.done): the journal, append-only, checked from its head; `blocks journal` as the pilot. Done 2026-10-31.
- [312-STO-0035](312-STO-0035-a-text-index-derived-from-a-journal.done): a text index derived from a journal, rebuilt equal to itself, a stale one told, every answer checked; `blocks index` as the pilot. Done 2026-10-31.
- [312-STO-0038](312-STO-0038-assertions-about-objects.done): assertions about objects, each with its type, source and interpretation, kept in a journal apart from content, mentioning its subject without retaining it; `blocks assert` as the pilot. Done 2026-10-31.
- [312-STO-0046](312-STO-0046-a-memory-domains-own-limit.done): a memory domain's own limit, set when it is made (MC-4.11, `blockstore.wit` 2.7). Done 2026-11-12.
- [312-STO-0047](312-STO-0047-a-vector-index-of-a-journals-embeddings.done): a vector index of a journal's embeddings by one model, an exact scan; `blocks vector` as the pilot. Done 2026-11-12.
- [312-STO-0049](312-STO-0049-a-domains-client-with-fewer-rights.done): a domain's client with fewer rights than its owner's (`blockstore.wit` 2.8), for a read-only `run -d` (312-APP-0134). Done 2026-11-12.

## Progress (2026-11-12)

- **The host criteria** are met by 312-STO-0034 (the journal's check from its head) and 312-STO-0035 and 0047 (an index rebuilt equal to itself, a stale one detected).
- **The QEMU criterion** waits for a program that holds a memory domain's client alone. Asked of the shell on 2026-11-12, now [312-APP-0134](312-APP-0134-a-program-started-in-a-memory-domain.done) (`run -d`); STO's check follows with `blocks` so started as the stand-in agent. The parts already run in QEMU are the `store` suite's domains check: two domains, one forgotten and its records collected, the other whole, a domain's client refused every domain call.
- **What the plan has that is not built:**
  - **A domain's term.** The termination condition MC-4.11 accepts in its place is there, `domain-forget`. A term the store keeps itself needs a calendar clock in `blockstore`, which holds no `rtc` client.
  - **Signed assertions** where provenance crosses a trust zone (Appendix B.3): none crosses one before [315](../issues/315-memory-across-machines.md).
  - **An approximate vector index** (HNSW) and an index of assertions by subject, when sizes ask for them.
  - **Embeddings made on the platform** by `NRL`'s runtime (900-NRL-0017).

## Acceptance criteria

- Host: the journal's check from its head; an index rebuilt equal to itself; a stale index detected.
- QEMU: a stand-in agent writes and reads its memory; forgetting frees what it should; another domain refused without a grant.

## Resolution

Its criteria are met.
- **Host:**
  - the journal's check from its head: 312-STO-0034;
  - an index rebuilt equal to itself, and a stale one detected: 312-STO-0035 (text) and 312-STO-0047 (vectors).
- **QEMU:** the `store` suite's `store_agent_check` on aarch64, on 4a69edb6 in this session's container (38 checks):
  - `blocks`, started by `run -d` (312-APP-0134) in a memory domain and holding that domain's client alone, writes its memory and reads it back (a journal, its text index, a claim);
  - the volume's names, another domain's and any other domain are out of its reach (`not-found`, `rights`), and the volume does not see its memory;
  - its domain forgotten by the owner, its memory is gone at once and a collection frees its records, while the other domain stands.

  x86's `store` suite (33 checks) makes no domain under qemu64, and so runs no agent.

**Its tasks,** all done: 312-STO-0034 (the journal), 0035 (a text index), 0038 (assertions), 0046 (a domain's limit), 0047 (a vector index) and 0049 (a domain's client with fewer rights, for a read-only `run -d`).

**What the plan has that was not built goes where it belongs:**
- **a domain's term:** [312-STO-0050](312-STO-0050-a-memory-domains-term.done), which waits for a choice of what a term's end does, then for a calendar clock in `blockstore`; the owner's `domain-forget` is the termination condition until then;
- **signed assertions** where provenance crosses a trust zone (Appendix B.3): [315](../issues/315-memory-across-machines.md)'s plan;
- **an approximate vector index** (HNSW) and an index of assertions by subject, when sizes ask: [310](../issues/310-the-index-on-the-medium.md)'s plan;
- **embeddings made on the platform:** `NRL`'s runtime (900-NRL-0017), for which the store's format is in `main` and NRL was told.

